   "note": "YEAR CONFLICT SETTLED, and decisively -- the title page carries TWO independent attestations of the same year. 'FOR THE SIXTY-FOURTH YEAR OF AMERICAN INDEPENDENCE' is 1775+64 = 1839, and the imprint prints '1839' outright. The catalog's 1816 is wrong. The page also states an approximate entry count ('amounting to near thirty-nine thousand') and an inclusion policy ('all heads of families, firms, and those doing business in the city'). It closes with an Othello parody: 'Who steals my purse steals trash; But he who BORROWS my DIRECTORY filches me Most villanously.'"
  },
